WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:09.302 --> 00:00:10.929
Tartt, edge of the area.

2
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.474
He has options. Chooses Rojas.

3
00:00:16.101 --> 00:00:18.520
What a goal! Great finish.

4
00:00:18.603 --> 00:00:21.356
You have to say, Chris,
from where they started the season,

5
00:00:21.439 --> 00:00:24.109
this Richmond team is unrecognizable!

6
00:00:24.192 --> 00:00:27.612
What a turnaround for AFC Richmond!

7
00:00:27.696 --> 00:00:31.866
And with that Dani Rojas goal, Richmond
are now on a four-game winning streak.

8
00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:33.743
They've certainly turned things around

9
00:00:33.827 --> 00:00:36.663
since adding their former captain
to the coaching staff, Wrighty?

10
00:00:36.746 --> 00:00:37.831
Absolutely, Seems.

11
00:00:37.914 --> 00:00:41.334
And watching Richmond play, you could
definitely see the Roy Kent effect.

12
00:00:41.418 --> 00:00:45.213
And that leads them nicely
into Saturday's FA Cup quarterfinal clash

13
00:00:45.297 --> 00:00:47.632
against Premiership side
Tottenham Hotspur.

14
00:00:47.716 --> 00:00:48.884
Yeah, good luck with that.

15
00:00:48.967 --> 00:00:51.595
It kills me to say it,
but Tottenham are a top top side.

16
00:00:51.678 --> 00:00:53.179
Unbelievable team.

17
00:00:53.263 --> 00:00:56.057
Coming up next,
we'll preview the quarterfinal

18
00:00:56.141 --> 00:00:58.351
between Bournemouth and Southampton.

19
00:00:58.435 --> 00:01:00.478
-Do you want a cup of tea?
-Yes, please.

20
00:01:07.944 --> 00:01:09.988
-Sugar?
-No, thank you.

21
00:01:11.573 --> 00:01:16.244
Luca, do you believe in guardian angels?

22
00:01:16.328 --> 00:01:18.413
Are they like Guardians of the Galaxy?

23
00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.793
Wait, are you naked in my kitchen?

24
00:01:24.502 --> 00:01:25.712
Wearing a smile.

25
00:01:26.254 --> 00:01:27.714
Put some clothes on!

26
00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:30.592
Mina the cleaner will be here any second.

27
00:01:35.263 --> 00:01:38.225
Mina. Do you want some tea?

28
00:01:38.808 --> 00:01:40.435
Will there be biscuits with that?

29
00:01:40.518 --> 00:01:41.519
Mother.

30
00:01:42.896 --> 00:01:43.897
Hello, darling.

31
00:01:44.731 --> 00:01:45.857
I've left your father.

32
00:01:47.984 --> 00:01:49.236
Wait, your mum's your cleaner?

33
00:01:49.319 --> 00:01:50.320
No.

34
00:01:50.987 --> 00:01:53.657
He doesn't listen to me.
He doesn't respect me.

35
00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:57.035
And Esther Perel says
it takes two people to create a pattern

36
00:01:57.118 --> 00:01:58.620
but only one to change it.

37
00:01:59.871 --> 00:02:01.248
I am that change.

38
00:02:01.331 --> 00:02:02.749
Good for you.

39
00:02:03.458 --> 00:02:05.961
Luca, will you please put some clothes on?

40
00:02:12.175 --> 00:02:13.593
I'll start in the study.

41
00:02:14.344 --> 00:02:15.637
Yes, thank you.

42
00:02:41.746 --> 00:02:44.958
Hey, Liza.
Saw your Instagram post on Sunday.

43
00:02:45.041 --> 00:02:46.751
Way to keep
that ice bucket challenge alive.

44
00:02:46.835 --> 00:02:48.837
-Morning.
-Hey, Derek.

45
00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:53.466
Great morning, Isabelle.

46
00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:54.634
-Yes.
-Hey, Ted.

47
00:02:54.718 --> 00:02:56.720
Hey, Liam.
Hey, tell your mom happy birthday for me.

48
00:02:56.803 --> 00:02:59.890
And whatever gift you end up getting her,
let her know it's from both of us, huh?

49
00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.270
-Morning. How y'all doing?
-Morning.

50
00:03:05.979 --> 00:03:08.440
You're doing great work, Colin.
And I love your new mantra.

51
00:03:08.523 --> 00:03:11.276
I'm a strong and capable man.
I am not a piece of shit.

52
00:03:11.359 --> 00:03:13.445
-You don't need the second part.
-Right.

53
00:03:13.528 --> 00:03:14.738
-Morning, Colin.
-Hey.

54
00:03:14.821 --> 00:03:16.489
Hey, Doc.
You get in any trouble last night?

55
00:03:17.073 --> 00:03:18.742
Nothing I care to speak about at work.

56
00:03:19.409 --> 00:03:21.453
Doc, you are more mysterious
than David Blaine

57
00:03:21.536 --> 00:03:23.955
reading a Sue Grafton novel at Area 51.

58
00:03:24.039 --> 00:03:26.374
Well, Ted, make an appointment
when you need to talk.

59
00:03:26.458 --> 00:03:27.667
Hey, I talk all the time, Doc.

60
00:03:27.751 --> 00:03:29.336
Just let me follow you around
for ten minutes.

61
00:03:29.419 --> 00:03:30.837
After five,
you'll want me to hush my butt.

62
00:03:31.838 --> 00:03:33.673
-Lookee here.
-Morning, Ted.

63
00:03:33.757 --> 00:03:36.259
Hey. I tell you what,
I'm shipping the heck out of you two.

64
00:03:37.427 --> 00:03:38.637
I'm calling HR.

65
00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:40.472
Yeah, well,
tell Mr. Pufnstuf I said hello.

66
00:03:41.097 --> 00:03:44.643
That is a joke
for people born in the early to mid '70s.

67
00:03:44.726 --> 00:03:48.438
And then they just
changed the shape of the tortellini…

68
00:03:49.189 --> 00:03:52.901
Well, I don't know about you fellas,
but I am fired up for this FA Cup thing.

69
00:03:52.984 --> 00:03:54.069
I mean, come on.

70
00:03:54.152 --> 00:03:56.613
A March Madness tournament
in the middle of our season

71
00:03:56.696 --> 00:03:58.907
featuring every dang team in the country?

72
00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:00.450
Yes, please.

73
00:04:00.533 --> 00:04:02.911
I mean, what we got?
Davids versus Goliaths, right?

74
00:04:02.994 --> 00:04:06.039
You know? Rockys versus Apollos.
Steve Wiebes against Billy Mitchells.

75
00:04:06.122 --> 00:04:08.375
-What's another one, Coach?
-Pearl Jam versus Ticketmaster.

76
00:04:08.458 --> 00:04:11.127
Classic battle of art
versus commerce right there. Yeah.

77
00:04:11.211 --> 00:04:12.462
I got a question for you though.

78
00:04:12.546 --> 00:04:15.590
Has a team not in the Premier League,
à la us, ever won the whole chimichanga?

79
00:04:15.674 --> 00:04:17.716
-Eight times.
-Eight times. Really?

80
00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:19.177
But not for 40 years.

81
00:04:20.345 --> 00:04:21.680
What have we got here?

82
00:04:21.763 --> 00:04:23.848
Uh-oh.
You back into floating office mode, huh?

83
00:04:23.932 --> 00:04:25.600
Yeah. But it's no bother.

84
00:04:25.684 --> 00:04:27.686
I'm a flaneur by nature.

85
00:04:28.311 --> 00:04:29.312
I get that, yeah.

86
00:04:29.396 --> 00:04:30.814
Hey, Coach, what's a flaneur?

87
00:04:30.897 --> 00:04:32.148
A wanderer.

88
00:04:32.941 --> 00:04:35.610
-What the fuck's wrong with you?
-Nothing.

89
00:04:37.112 --> 00:04:38.530
Jane and I got back together.

90
00:04:39.281 --> 00:04:40.657
-Great news.
-Well, that's nice.

91
00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:43.201
-Fantastic.
-How about that. Look at you guys.

92
00:04:43.702 --> 00:04:45.579
Do you really think that's a good idea?

93
00:04:53.503 --> 00:04:55.380
Shit. Two missed calls from her.

94
00:04:55.463 --> 00:04:56.590
Be right back!

95
00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:01.803
I'd like to request an emergency meeting
of the Diamond Dogs.

96
00:05:01.887 --> 00:05:03.138
Diamond Dogs, mount up.

97
00:05:04.514 --> 00:05:06.641
-Hey, Roy, you wanna sit in with us?
-No.

98
00:05:06.725 --> 00:05:08.351
Okay. Yeah, shut that.

99
00:05:10.729 --> 00:05:11.730
He looks a little bit--

100
00:05:11.813 --> 00:05:14.399
Yeah, you're gonna come in through here.
That's fine. I got you.

101
00:05:14.482 --> 00:05:15.650
Just-- Do you wanna--

102
00:05:15.734 --> 00:05:16.693
Dukes of Hazzard style,

103
00:05:16.776 --> 00:05:18.778
or as you guys probably call it,
"the Earls of Risk."

104
00:05:18.862 --> 00:05:21.114
-Just go round.
-Yeah. Why don't you come legs first?

105
00:05:21.197 --> 00:05:22.449
You wanna-- You wanna jump in?

106
00:05:22.532 --> 00:05:24.409
You'd be in here if you just went round.

107
00:05:24.492 --> 00:05:26.661
-Ready? Here he comes. Right--
-I'm just gonna stay here.

108
00:05:26.745 --> 00:05:28.413
That's fine. Good idea. Probably best.

109
00:05:28.496 --> 00:05:32.125
All right. Okay, Higgiebottoms,
you called this puppy, so start barking.

110
00:05:32.208 --> 00:05:35.879
Well, I'm just not sure that
Jane and Beard are very healthy together.

111
00:05:35.962 --> 00:05:37.797
And I'm a little bit disappointed

112
00:05:37.881 --> 00:05:40.175
that neither of you backed me up
when I just said so.

113
00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:42.928
Okay. Calling us out.

114
00:05:43.011 --> 00:05:45.096
I appreciate that and I hear you, but--

115
00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:48.058
I mean, in my defense,
I know why I didn't say anything.

116
00:05:48.141 --> 00:05:50.769
-And why's that?
-'Cause you should never say anything.

117
00:05:50.852 --> 00:05:52.646
And look, man,
I learned that the hard way.

118
00:05:52.729 --> 00:05:55.690
One of my best friends growing up
was this fella, Marcus Girard.

119
00:05:55.774 --> 00:05:59.486
He dated the same girl from grade school
to high school to college, whole time.

120
00:05:59.569 --> 00:06:02.572
And she could be a little bit of a pill,
if I'm being honest, you know?

121
00:06:02.656 --> 00:06:03.907
No reason to start lying now.

122
00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:06.868
And, well, I let him know that.
I told him so.

123
00:06:06.952 --> 00:06:09.371
And he was not too pleased, all right?

124
00:06:09.454 --> 00:06:11.873
And that is the last time
I ever gave a best man speech.

125
00:06:11.957 --> 00:06:15.460
I mean, yeah, I try to be
outwardly supportive of all relationships

126
00:06:15.544 --> 00:06:17.754
due to my dad
sabotaging one of my first loves.

127
00:06:18.505 --> 00:06:21.675
In year four, he sat me
and my classmate, Nadia Shookums, down

128
00:06:21.758 --> 00:06:24.177
in the living room and said
he thought we could both do better.

129
00:06:25.512 --> 00:06:27.180
Well, she listened to him.

130
00:06:27.264 --> 00:06:29.641
Boy, that's a heaping spoonful
of truth soup right there.

131
00:06:29.724 --> 00:06:30.892
Yeah. I know.

132
00:06:30.976 --> 00:06:32.894
Look, Higgins,
I just think it's bad business

133
00:06:32.978 --> 00:06:35.647
to get all up
in anyone else's business, you know?

134
00:06:36.273 --> 00:06:38.108
Okay, I understand.

135
00:06:39.818 --> 00:06:42.779
So even though this is an unsanctioned
meeting because Beard wasn't here,

136
00:06:42.862 --> 00:06:44.698
let's just go ahead
and Diamond Dogs dismount.

137
00:06:49.661 --> 00:06:51.204
Stupid barking means it's over, right?

138
00:06:51.288 --> 00:06:52.289
Yes, sir. Welcome back.

139
00:06:52.372 --> 00:06:55.041
-Ay, ay, ay. That was a doozy.
-What's wrong?

140
00:06:55.125 --> 00:06:57.752
Jane's roommate flipped out on her.

141
00:06:57.836 --> 00:06:59.296
-Kicked her out of the house.
-Oh, no.

142
00:06:59.379 --> 00:07:01.590
So now she's moving in with me.

143
00:07:02.465 --> 00:07:03.300
That's good.

144
00:07:03.383 --> 00:07:05.135
That's great news. Congratulations.

145
00:07:06.303 --> 00:07:08.054
Thanks, guys.

146
00:07:18.857 --> 00:07:20.650
All right. Chin up, lads.

147
00:07:20.734 --> 00:07:22.527
Come on, Colin. You dolt.

148
00:07:23.695 --> 00:07:25.906
Colin, you're leaning too far back.

149
00:07:25.989 --> 00:07:27.657
Head down, fucking whip it.

150
00:07:29.075 --> 00:07:30.994
I am a strong and capable man.

151
00:07:31.077 --> 00:07:32.329
Thanks, Roy.

152
00:07:32.412 --> 00:07:34.372
Bumbercatch, great pass,

153
00:07:34.456 --> 00:07:36.291
but it don't mean shit
if they see it coming.

154
00:07:36.374 --> 00:07:38.376
The rest of you in the box,
when the shot goes,

155
00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:39.878
you fucking follow it in.

156
00:07:39.961 --> 00:07:42.047
Yeah, you smell that, lads?

157
00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:43.423
That's the Roy Kent effect.

158
00:07:45.467 --> 00:07:48.428
-Roy Kent! Roy Kent!
-Roy Kent!

159
00:07:53.683 --> 00:07:54.893
Anything for me, coach?

160
00:07:57.854 --> 00:07:59.022
All right, let's go again.

161
00:08:02.984 --> 00:08:05.654
Hey, Roy. You know you're paid
to coach the whole team, right?

162
00:08:06.154 --> 00:08:09.074
No, no, that's fine.
Just take 4% off my paycheck.

163
00:08:09.699 --> 00:08:10.700
Ted!

164
00:08:11.451 --> 00:08:12.994
-Ted!
-You hear that?

165
00:08:14.996 --> 00:08:16.081
Hey!

166
00:08:16.164 --> 00:08:18.416
Do you have lunch plans?

167
00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:20.544
As a matter of fact, I do, yeah.

168
00:08:20.627 --> 00:08:23.713
Coach Beard and I here
are doing Secret Sandwich Switcheroo

169
00:08:23.797 --> 00:08:24.965
every other Friday.

170
00:08:25.048 --> 00:08:28.260
-What we do is I make a sandwich--
-I don't care, Ted.

171
00:08:28.343 --> 00:08:30.887
You're coming to lunch
with me and my mother.

172
00:08:30.971 --> 00:08:32.138
Okay. Sounds great.

173
00:08:33.306 --> 00:08:35.140
Spoiler alert. I made you a BLT.

174
00:08:35.225 --> 00:08:36.810
-Samesies.
-What?

175
00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:40.020
Crown & Anchor at 2:00.

176
00:08:40.105 --> 00:08:41.106
Okay.

177
00:08:42.065 --> 00:08:45.026
I look forward to lunching with you, Ted.

178
00:08:45.110 --> 00:08:46.820
Hi, Rebecca's mom.

179
00:08:46.903 --> 00:08:48.405
Hey, fellas. Say hi.

180
00:08:48.488 --> 00:08:50.448
Hi, Rebecca's mum.

181
00:08:50.532 --> 00:08:51.950
Hello, boys.

182
00:08:52.033 --> 00:08:55.120
And the name's not Rebecca's mum,
it's Deborah.

183
00:08:55.203 --> 00:08:57.038
I'm a work in progress,

184
00:08:57.122 --> 00:08:59.833
a voracious book on tape listener

185
00:08:59.916 --> 00:09:04.004
and a staunch believer
that if you get dealt lemons in life,

186
00:09:04.087 --> 00:09:06.923
then you should make
lemon lavender mojitos.

187
00:09:07.007 --> 00:09:08.008
Mum!

188
00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:10.552
Nice to meet you, Deborah.

189
00:09:12.262 --> 00:09:14.848
Boy, I love meeting people's moms.

190
00:09:14.931 --> 00:09:17.517
It's like reading an instruction manual
as to why they're nuts.

191
00:09:17.601 --> 00:09:19.519
Let's go!

192
00:09:20.145 --> 00:09:21.605
How's Mrs. Beard doing, by the way?

193
00:09:21.688 --> 00:09:23.648
-Full-blown QAnon.
-Yep.

194
00:09:26.818 --> 00:09:30.322
-Hey, look alive, Coach.
-Thank you.

195
00:09:30.989 --> 00:09:32.866
-No horseradish?
-I thought you were allergic?

196
00:09:32.949 --> 00:09:34.200
To horses and radishes.

197
00:09:34.284 --> 00:09:35.285
I'm sorry.

198
00:09:35.827 --> 00:09:37.120
-Hi, guys.
-Hey.

199
00:09:37.203 --> 00:09:40.248
Ted. Do you reckon you'd be up for
driving us back from lunch?

200
00:09:40.332 --> 00:09:41.458
Sure, I'll give it a shot.

201
00:09:41.541 --> 00:09:43.209
I've got some creative work
I wanna do this afternoon

202
00:09:43.293 --> 00:09:44.669
and I kinda wanna be
a little buzzed for it.

203
00:09:44.753 --> 00:09:47.422
-Seems like a great idea all around.
-Thank you.

204
00:09:49.007 --> 00:09:50.300
One second here.

205
00:09:50.383 --> 00:09:51.384
Hello?

206
00:09:52.219 --> 00:09:53.220
This is him.

207
00:09:54.429 --> 00:09:56.681
W-- Is he okay?

208
00:09:58.808 --> 00:10:00.477
Okay. Okay. I'll--

209
00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:03.104
Well, I mean, that's gonna be
a little tricky 'cause I'm at work.

210
00:10:04.272 --> 00:10:05.565
No, I work in London.

211
00:10:06.066 --> 00:10:07.943
Yeah, no, it's a heck of a commute.

212
00:10:08.026 --> 00:10:10.654
Tell you what.
How about I call my wife-- his mom,

213
00:10:10.737 --> 00:10:11.988
and then I'll see--

214
00:10:13.365 --> 00:10:14.616
She's pulling up right now?

215
00:10:15.116 --> 00:10:17.827
Okay, well, there you go. Crisis averted.

216
00:10:17.911 --> 00:10:20.622
Okay. All right now. Have fun. Bye.

217
00:10:23.541 --> 00:10:24.960
Everything okay?

218
00:10:25.585 --> 00:10:26.586
Yeah, yeah.

219
00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:29.381
No, Henry forgot his lunch today
for his field trip.

220
00:10:29.464 --> 00:10:31.591
But, no, Michelle's there.
So, yeah, we're all good.

221
00:10:33.510 --> 00:10:34.553
Hi, Keeley.

222
00:10:34.636 --> 00:10:36.805
You got to tell Roy
he needs to start coaching me.

223
00:10:37.472 --> 00:10:39.975
Wait. You want me to tell Roy Kent
what to do?

224
00:10:40.058 --> 00:10:42.477
-That's a great idea.
-Yeah, he's gonna love that.

225
00:10:42.561 --> 00:10:44.980
Yeah, I'll totally drop it
into one of our many conversations

226
00:10:45.063 --> 00:10:47.941
where Roy talks to me about his life
and asks for my advice.

227
00:10:52.529 --> 00:10:53.822
Philistines!

228
00:10:53.905 --> 00:10:55.824
-Philistines.
-I'm asking for help here.

229
00:10:55.907 --> 00:10:57.576
Jamie, you and Roy got your own history.

230
00:10:57.659 --> 00:10:59.452
Y'all got to get together and woman up.

231
00:11:00.787 --> 00:11:02.038
I think you mean man up, mate.

232
00:11:02.872 --> 00:11:05.750
No, y'all have been manning up
for a while. Look where that's got you.

233
00:11:05.834 --> 00:11:08.003
Keeley, you got any advice
for this young, half-dressed fella

234
00:11:08.086 --> 00:11:09.504
on how to get through to Roy?

235
00:11:09.588 --> 00:11:10.755
I agree.

236
00:11:11.631 --> 00:11:13.758
That's a confusing way to answer
that question. Am I wrong?

237
00:11:14.676 --> 00:11:16.094
No, I mean, I agree with Roy.

238
00:11:16.636 --> 00:11:18.513
Just agree
with everything that he throws at you.

239
00:11:18.597 --> 00:11:20.515
Really takes the anger wind
out of his brat sails.

240
00:11:22.017 --> 00:11:23.518
-Shall we?
-Yes, ma'am.

241
00:11:24.394 --> 00:11:26.605
-All right. Bon voyage.
-Bye, Jamie!

242
00:11:34.946 --> 00:11:36.448
I don't really know how to talk to you.

243
00:11:37.532 --> 00:11:38.909
Then it's working.

244
00:11:42.412 --> 00:11:44.706
You're gonna wanna look up "Philistines."

245
