495
00:26:54.699 --> 00:26:56.701
Or put Sam and go three up front?

496
00:26:56.785 --> 00:26:58.787
I don't--
We gotta be aggressive here, right?

497
00:26:59.287 --> 00:27:00.413
I think we need--

498
00:27:01.331 --> 00:27:04.251
Reynolds, Winchester, Babatunde,
you're going in.

499
00:27:06.211 --> 00:27:08.588
Hey! Colin, Dani, Richard,

500
00:27:09.548 --> 00:27:10.423
you're coming off.

501
00:27:10.507 --> 00:27:12.050
-Me?
-Yes, you, Colin.

502
00:27:12.133 --> 00:27:13.260
What's going on?

503
00:27:14.135 --> 00:27:15.845
-Park the bus!
-What?

504
00:27:15.929 --> 00:27:17.180
Park the bus!

505
00:27:17.264 --> 00:27:18.682
No one up front. Do it.

506
00:27:18.765 --> 00:27:21.268
-But we need a goal!
-Park the goddamn bus! Go!

507
00:27:22.143 --> 00:27:24.271
Park the bus! Park the bus!

508
00:27:25.105 --> 00:27:28.108
And it's a rare triple substitution
for Richmond.

509
00:27:28.191 --> 00:27:29.901
-Park the bus!
-Park the bus!

510
00:27:29.985 --> 00:27:31.695
-What's going on?
-I got this.

511
00:27:32.279 --> 00:27:34.573
Looks like
the coaching staff are panicking, Arlo.

512
00:27:34.656 --> 00:27:37.158
This is what a fish pie can do to a team.

513
00:27:39.286 --> 00:27:40.287
Ted?

514
00:27:40.370 --> 00:27:42.998
Stoppage time now,
and Richmond are completely dropping back.

515
00:27:43.081 --> 00:27:45.125
-They're playing very defensively.
-Ted?

516
00:27:45.208 --> 00:27:47.544
Richmond going for a draw
is a big mistake, Arlo.

517
00:27:47.627 --> 00:27:50.380
You're the underdog.
You're at home. You go for the win.

518
00:27:50.463 --> 00:27:53.091
-Wait, disaster for Spurs!
-Ted?

519
00:27:53.174 --> 00:27:57.012
A slip by Barnett and Richmond
are on the counterattack!

520
00:27:58.054 --> 00:28:01.308
Obisanya loops
a perfect diagonal ball to Tartt.

521
00:28:01.391 --> 00:28:03.018
He shoots!

522
00:28:03.101 --> 00:28:05.270
Tartt buries it in the back of the net!

523
00:28:05.353 --> 00:28:08.440
Richmond, impossibly, are on top!

524
00:28:14.112 --> 00:28:15.322
Oh, Ted.

525
00:28:23.622 --> 00:28:25.206
Yes!

526
00:28:29.127 --> 00:28:30.879
-Hey, boss. Congrats.
-Yeah.

527
00:28:30.962 --> 00:28:32.923
-Where's Ted?
-I don't know.

528
00:28:33.006 --> 00:28:35.050
A stomach thing.
I'll check in on my way home.

529
00:28:35.133 --> 00:28:36.301
Great. Thank you.

530
00:28:37.177 --> 00:28:39.179
-Congratulations.
-Congratulations.

531
00:28:39.262 --> 00:28:42.307
It's good to see
the Roy Kent effect is alive and well.

532
00:28:42.390 --> 00:28:44.226
Nothing to do with me. That is all Nate.

533
00:28:44.309 --> 00:28:46.311
We're Richmond till we die!

534
00:28:46.394 --> 00:28:49.606
We know we are! We're sure we are!
We're Richmond till we die!

535
00:28:51.274 --> 00:28:53.568
Congratulations on a thrilling win.

536
00:28:54.152 --> 00:28:55.445
Yeah, thank you. Thank you very much.

537
00:28:55.528 --> 00:28:57.405
-What happened to Ted?
-I don't know.

538
00:28:57.489 --> 00:28:58.573
Food poisoning or something?

539
00:28:58.657 --> 00:29:01.076
It seemed like a negative strategy
to pull everyone into defense

540
00:29:01.159 --> 00:29:02.160
when you needed a goal.

541
00:29:02.244 --> 00:29:03.787
Yes, but I knew they needed a goal too.

542
00:29:03.870 --> 00:29:05.538
As long as I made sure
they couldn't get through,

543
00:29:05.622 --> 00:29:07.457
at some point, human nature,
someone would screw up

544
00:29:07.540 --> 00:29:08.667
and we could exploit that.

545
00:29:08.750 --> 00:29:09.960
Brilliant!

546
00:29:10.043 --> 00:29:11.211
You said he was a lemon.

547
00:29:11.294 --> 00:29:14.005
-Impressive by an assistant coach.
-Just did what had to be done.

548
00:29:14.089 --> 00:29:16.007
It's not like
I'm some kind of "wonder kid."

549
00:29:16.091 --> 00:29:18.093
-Some kind of what?
-"Wonder kid."

550
00:29:18.176 --> 00:29:20.178
I think you mean wunderkind. Yeah?

551
00:29:21.221 --> 00:29:22.514
Yeah.

552
00:29:22.597 --> 00:29:24.182
Can we fix that with editing, or--

553
00:29:24.266 --> 00:29:25.475
No, we're live.

554
00:29:25.559 --> 00:29:28.895
Well, great job by Nathan Shelley,
the wonder kid.

555
00:29:28.979 --> 00:29:31.147
-And we wish Ted a speedy recovery.
-Yeah.

556
00:29:31.231 --> 00:29:33.733
-Thank you. Yeah.
-No, thank you. Thank you. Just go.

557
00:29:36.152 --> 00:29:39.531
As someone who cares about you,
I'm concerned that you and Jane are…

558
00:29:43.076 --> 00:29:44.828
Look, let me ask you one question.

559
00:29:45.745 --> 00:29:48.039
You're a great man.
Does Jane make you greater?

560
00:29:51.835 --> 00:29:53.795
Okay, look, I apologize.

561
00:29:59.968 --> 00:30:02.554
Okay, okay. That--

562
00:30:03.096 --> 00:30:04.848
I hear you. I get it.

563
00:30:06.641 --> 00:30:08.643
-We will never speak of this again.
-No, no.

564
00:30:12.564 --> 00:30:14.232
-See you Monday.
-See you Monday. Yep.

565
00:30:25.619 --> 00:30:27.078
I missed that scared face.

566
00:30:27.662 --> 00:30:28.955
I missed you too.

567
00:30:29.497 --> 00:30:30.582
How was Finn?

568
00:30:31.458 --> 00:30:32.918
He's like a Rembrandt.

569
00:30:33.001 --> 00:30:36.129
Beautiful to look at but so dim.

570
00:30:38.340 --> 00:30:39.382
Try this.

571
00:30:42.427 --> 00:30:44.346
-Yeah, much better. Yeah.
-Yeah?

572
00:30:44.429 --> 00:30:46.514
It's not too Oliver Twist?

573
00:30:46.598 --> 00:30:49.226
Well, it is,
but that's kind of my kink, so--

574
00:30:49.309 --> 00:30:50.894
"May I have some more?"

575
00:31:01.029 --> 00:31:03.990
Nate, great fucking work today.

576
00:31:04.074 --> 00:31:05.242
Thanks, Roy.

577
00:31:18.672 --> 00:31:20.006
Dr. Sharon!

578
00:31:20.090 --> 00:31:21.883
We're going for a drink. Will you join us?

579
00:31:21.967 --> 00:31:25.345
Wait, are we even allowed to talk to you
at night? If not, I'm so sorry.

580
00:31:25.971 --> 00:31:28.682
For a quarterfinal win,
you get me for one drink.

581
00:31:30.100 --> 00:31:31.393
I'll see you after.

582
00:31:41.236 --> 00:31:42.737
Wait for the beep.

583
00:31:42.821 --> 00:31:45.448
You gotta leave your name,
you gotta leave your number.

584
00:31:46.157 --> 00:31:47.450
Hey, Ted, it's me.

585
00:31:49.202 --> 00:31:51.788
I was a bit worried about you today.
Hope you're okay.

586
00:31:52.747 --> 00:31:56.543
If you need me,
just please do give me a call.

587
00:31:58.128 --> 00:31:59.254
It's just, I'm on my way home

588
00:31:59.337 --> 00:32:01.006
for a very difficult conversation
with my mother,

589
00:32:01.089 --> 00:32:03.550
and I could really do with
one of your pep talks.

590
00:32:04.718 --> 00:32:05.719
Anyway…

591
00:32:06.887 --> 00:32:07.971
take care.

592
00:32:16.521 --> 00:32:17.522
Mum!

593
00:32:21.776 --> 00:32:23.069
Mum!

594
00:32:26.197 --> 00:32:27.240
Mum?

595
00:32:35.081 --> 00:32:39.419
"Darling, sorry to miss you. Your father
apologized and bought me a new Tesla.

596
00:32:42.088 --> 00:32:44.090
I'll take you for a spin in it
next time I visit.

597
00:32:44.174 --> 00:32:47.427
PS, shepherd's pie is in the fridge.
Needs two minutes in the microwave."

598
00:33:06.571 --> 00:33:07.697
Hey, Luca.

599
00:33:08.448 --> 00:33:10.659
Yes, it's an actual phone call.

600
00:33:11.201 --> 00:33:12.661
No, I haven't been arrested.

601
00:33:13.245 --> 00:33:15.872
I just thought you'd like to know
that my parents are away.

602
00:33:16.414 --> 00:33:17.624
So we could--

603
00:33:18.291 --> 00:33:19.876
Exactly.

604
00:33:19.960 --> 00:33:21.044
See you soon.

605
00:33:34.891 --> 00:33:37.811
Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman
Them boys up to something

606
00:33:37.894 --> 00:33:40.438
They just spent like two or three weeks
Out the country

607
00:33:40.522 --> 00:33:42.482
-You know all the lyrics.
-Them boys up to something

608
00:33:42.566 --> 00:33:44.150
They just not just bluffin'

609
00:33:44.734 --> 00:33:47.279
You don't have to call
I hit my dance like Usher

610
00:33:47.362 --> 00:33:50.156
-Oy, put your phone away, mate.
-Yes, yes, yes. Okay, okay. Sorry.

611
00:33:50.240 --> 00:33:51.241
Carry on going. You're great.

612
00:33:51.324 --> 00:33:54.411
I just found my tempo
Like I'm DJ Mustard

613
00:33:54.494 --> 00:33:57.789
I hit that Ginóbili
With my left hand up like

614
00:34:07.841 --> 00:34:08.967
Ted, you scared me.

615
00:34:13.346 --> 00:34:14.347
Are you okay?

616
00:34:18.934 --> 00:34:20.436
I wanna make an appointment.

